<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What lint says about a phone and this is not one.

  Anything genuinely wrong is left to be reported. These two are checks whose whole subject is
  absent on a television, and left on they are three lines of noise in every report -- which is how
  a real finding comes to be scrolled past.
-->
<lint>
    <!--
      About the photo picker Android 14 gives a viewer who wants to grant access to some pictures
      rather than all of them. This app asks for video and audio and never for images, and a
      television has no picker to show anyway: the permission screen there is a yes or a no.
    -->
    <issue id="SelectedPhotoAccess" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      The mark this app is listed by exists at xhdpi, which is the density a television panel
      reports. Copies at the densities of a phone would be bytes in the download for screens that
      cannot be a television.
    -->
    <issue id="IconMissingDensityFolder" severity="ignore" />
</lint>
